---
/**
 * The island: five things, a walking time, and what is wrong with each of them.
 *
 * Sixty hectares with one house, a ruin, some kilns and a lot of birds. A letting site would
 * call this "wild beauty on your doorstep". The useful version is a list with distances and the
 * reason each place is a bad idea at the wrong point of the tide, because on an island where the
 * road disappears the walking times and the state of the water are the same question.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import { ISLAND, FACTS } from '../data/house';
import { SEASON_FACTS, hoursLabel } from '../lib/season';
---
<Base
  title="The island — Hallowsand"
  description="Sixty hectares, one house, a roofless chapel, three lime kilns and the north ledges. Walking times from the door and what each place is like at the wrong point of the tide."
  section="The island"
>
  <section>
    <div class="page doc doc--text">
      <div class="rail">
        <div>
          <p class="rail__k">Size</p>
          <span class="rail__n">{FACTS.hectares} ha</span>
          <p class="rail__v">about forty minutes end to end, at a walk</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="rail__k">Buildings</p>
          <span class="rail__n">1</span>
          <p class="rail__v">plus a roofless chapel and three abandoned kilns</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="rail__k">Roads</p>
          <span class="rail__n">0</span>
          <p class="rail__v">a track from the landing to the house, and nothing else</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <p class="label">The island</p>
        <h1 class="display">Sixty hectares, and you will have walked all of it by Wednesday.</h1>
        <p class="stand">
          That is not a complaint. Knowing a place completely is a different holiday from seeing
          a lot of one, and it is the one on offer here.
        </p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Five things worth walking to, with how long they take from the door. Each has
            something wrong with it, and the wrong things are more useful than the right ones:
            the ledges cut you off from above, the chapel field is full of birds that will make
            their feelings clear, and the kilns are a drop with no fence.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {ISLAND.map((feature, index) => (
    <section>
      <div class="page doc">
        <div class="rail">
          <div>
            <p class="rail__k">Walk</p>
            <span class="rail__n">{feature.walk.split(' —')[0]}</span>
            {feature.walk.includes('—') && <p class="rail__v">{feature.walk.split('— ')[1]}</p>}
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="rail__k">No.</p>
            <span class="rail__n">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <p class="rail__v">of {ISLAND.length}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col">
          <h2 class="head">{feature.name}</h2>
          <p class="prose">{feature.note}</p>
        </div>
        {feature.photo && (
          <div class="full isl__p">
            <Photo slug={feature.photo} width="full" band loading={index < 2 ? 'eager' : 'lazy'} />
          </div>
        )}
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <section>
    <div class="page doc doc--text">
      <div class="rail">
        <div>
          <p class="rail__k">Shut, per day</p>
          <span class="rail__n">{hoursLabel(SEASON_FACTS.meanShutPerDay)}</span>
          <p class="rail__v">which is the walking budget, not the daylight</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h2 class="head">Walking and the tide are the same question.</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Everything on this page is on the island, so none of it depends on the causeway. What
            does depend on the tide is the ledges — walk them at the start of a closure, not the
            end — and anything involving the mainland, which is most things.
          </p>
          <p>
            The practical rule guests arrive at by about day three is to do the long walk while
            the road is shut, because there is nothing else you could have been doing with those
            hours anyway. <a class="u" href="/crossing">The crossing table</a> is on the kitchen
            wall for the same reason.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .isl__p { margin-top: var(--s6); }
</style>
